# Portfolio Manager — private source repository
#
# This repository is PRIVATE and holds everything: the application, the migrations, the
# documentation, the test harness and the build tooling.
#
# The hosted site is served from a SEPARATE PUBLIC repository, which receives only the
# files a browser actually asks for. That copy is built into deploy/ by
#
#     node BUILD-DEPLOY-SET.mjs --sync deploy
#
# and pushed from there. Nothing explanatory reaches it, because nothing explanatory is in
# the set it copies.
#
# So the rule here is no longer "keep the design out" — it is only, and still,
# NEVER COMMIT PORTFOLIO DATA. Real project, people and financial records do not belong in
# any repository, private or otherwise.

# Backups and exports contain real project, people and financial records.
portfolio-manager-backup-*.json
portfolio-manager-audit-archive-*.json
*-backup-*.json
*.dump
*.sql.gz

# Database dumps
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/

# Full-build archives. The repo IS the build; a committed ZIP is a stale duplicate.
PPM-Tool-*.zip
*.zip

# The public working copy lives OUTSIDE this folder, at ..\ppm-proof-of-concept, because
# GitHub Desktop refuses to manage a repository nested inside another one. This rule stays
# for the old location: if anything ever writes deploy\ in here again, it must not be
# committed - two copies of the application in one repository defeats the split.
deploy/

# Office lock files, created while a workbook is open.
.~lock.*#
~$*

# Local scratch
localhost.txt
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/
